.TH BUDGET 1
.SH NAME
budget \- TempleOS budget ledger
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/budget
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Budget
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Apps/Budget
ledger.
It runs under
.IR wm (1),
in the TempleOS 8x8 font and 16-color palette.
.PP
The ledger holds dated entries, each moving an
.I amount
from a
.I credit
(from) account to a
.I debit
(to) account.
Every row shows, in the original's layout,
.IP
.EX
date credit debit:balance amount:desc
.EE
.PP
where
.I balance
is the running balance of the
.I view account
(initially
.BR BANK ):
crediting the view account subtracts, debiting it adds.
Rows are colored by the credit account's color and kept sorted by date.
.PP
Entries are added and edited in the form strip:
Date, Amount, Credit(from)Acct, Debit(to)Acct, Desc, then
.B Ok
(or Enter in any field).
Leaving credit or debit blank offers the account picker,
as the original form does.
A date may be given as
.IB mm / dd / yy
or
.IB mm / dd / yyyy
(two-digit years above 2050 are taken as the previous century),
or as one of
.TP
.B *
today (also the empty string)
.TP
.B [
the date of the first entry
.TP
.B ]
the date of the last entry
.PD
.PP
Periodic
.I templates
generate scheduled copies of an entry between a start and an end date.
The types are Interval (every
.I period
days), Monthly, Bimonthly, Semiannual and Annual.
Template-generated rows appear in the ledger but are not saved;
pressing Enter on one edits its template,
and deleting one deletes the whole template with all its copies.
.SS Keys and menus
The File, Edit and View menus carry the same commands as the original.
With the ledger focused:
.TP
.B n
new entry
.TP
.B c
copy the current row into a new entry
.TP
.B p
periodic: expand a schedule starting at the current row once into real
entries (the first occurrence is skipped; it is the row itself)
.TP
.B t
new template
.TP
.B Enter
edit the current row in place (a template copy edits its template)
.TP
.B Ctrl-Y
delete the current row (a template copy deletes its template and copies)
.TP
.B a
edit the accounts: one per line, a color number 0\-15 then the name
.TP
.B v
choose the view account from the picker
.TP
.B up/down, mouse
move the current row
.TP
.B Esc, q
exit, saving the ledger
.PD
.PP
.B File\(->Abort
exits without saving (the original's Shift-Esc).
All other exits, including the window's close control, save first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $home/lib/temple-budget.txt
accounts, templates and entries, tab-separated
.TP
.B /tmp/temple-budget.txt
fallback when there is no home
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/budget.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The DolDoc popup forms and menus are rendered as Tk strips and panels;
Ok or Enter submits them, where TempleOS submitted forms with Esc.
Shift-Esc cannot be distinguished on the keyboard channel, so abort
without saving is only on the File menu.
.PP
Persistence is a text file, not the original's
.B Bgt.DATA.Z
binary and string table, and account colors live in it rather than in
.BR Accts.DD.Z .
